# P2 hard-state captures: per-machine corpus, never repo content.
#
# Same rule as `soak/` next door and for a stronger reason. Every record here
# embeds a FULL wire state -- hands, decks, enemy intents, relic descriptions
# -- so a committed capture would put a slab of the shipped game's own strings
# in the repo, and the seeds are read-back (R95) so nobody else can reproduce
# one anyway. Cite a capture by path from a review packet.
#
# The records are also stamped with the trigger DEFINITION that produced them
# (`placeholder-conservative-2026-08-13` until [USER] rules -- see
# review/active/p2-hard-state-thresholds-2026-08-13.md), which is what lets a
# corpus be filtered rather than thrown away when the numbers move.
#
# Schema: understudy/p2capture.py.
*
!.gitignore
